From e1100d4bc78b88e1e2776c474b01cbfbe90a16b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:27:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Pitch: under the 65% floor, show only the films that
 clear it, with "Show lower matches" (rule 1700)

Owner change, build 38: no auto-fill below the match floor. When fewer than seven clear 65% shown
match, only those show and a quiet line under the last row says "Only 2 films match you 65% or
more for this." (none: "Nothing here matches you 65% or more.") with the text button "Show lower
matches", which re-ranks this ask free with op "rank" `floor: false`, up to seven at their real %.
Later re-ranks of the same ask keep it off; a new pitch starts with it on. The earlier
"closest are here too" fallback is gone. Web and iPhone; rule 1700, its check, the DS log and docs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013WRDCFXH8nihP92apJAVW7
