-- **Before → after:** (1) `rankRecut` returned `opts.limit ?? 24` films; now `PITCH_SHORTLIST` (7), only as many as fit, never padded. (2) Signed in with a profile there was no shown-match floor on Pitch (rule 1119's `MATCH_FLOOR` 55 stored only drops films while 24 others remain); now the first 24 of the order get their canonical match and a film under 65% SHOWN (`shownMatch`, lib/taste/shown-match.ts) is left out (no match yet: kept; "so bad it's good": exempt); when fewer than 3 clear it, the best there are show with a plain note. (3) `unseen` / `seenOk` / `rewatch` became `seen: "new" | "either" | "rewatch"` and `loved`. New to me and Either rank exactly as the old default and `seenOk` did. Rewatch without Ones you loved is new: every film the viewer has seen is the pool, lifted by the old comfort-rewatch bonus (rating and age) so loved films lead; Ones you loved is the old `rewatch` (4.5★+ or hearted, warmth up, bleakness down). The friend's seen films are left out when "new" is set in so many words (typed, or picked on the count line), as `unseen` did. (4) The keyword parser and the model's anchor drop a leading language word ("Korean Parasite" → anchor Parasite, language ko; "French Kiss" kept whole). (5) An anchor that does not resolve is no longer a "Not used" word: the route asks "Which film did you mean?" with up to three typo-close titles (lib/search-typo.ts over lib/top-titles.ts) and ranks the rest of the ask.
+- **Before → after:** (1) `rankRecut` returned `opts.limit ?? 24` films; now `PITCH_SHORTLIST` (7), only as many as fit, never padded. (2) Signed in with a profile there was no shown-match floor on Pitch (rule 1119's `MATCH_FLOOR` 55 stored only drops films while 24 others remain); now the first 24 of the order get their canonical match and a film under 65% SHOWN (`shownMatch`, lib/taste/shown-match.ts) is left out (no match yet: kept; "so bad it's good": exempt), and nothing lower fills its place; fewer than seven clearing it, the clients say so ("Only 2 films match you 65% or more for this.") with "Show lower matches", which re-ranks that ask with the floor off (op "rank" `floor: false`), up to seven at their real %. (Amended the same day by the owner: an earlier draft filled in the best below the floor whenever fewer than three cleared it.) (3) `unseen` / `seenOk` / `rewatch` became `seen: "new" | "either" | "rewatch"` and `loved`. New to me and Either rank exactly as the old default and `seenOk` did. Rewatch without Ones you loved is new: every film the viewer has seen is the pool, lifted by the old comfort-rewatch bonus (rating and age) so loved films lead; Ones you loved is the old `rewatch` (4.5★+ or hearted, warmth up, bleakness down). The friend's seen films are left out when "new" is set in so many words (typed, or picked on the count line), as `unseen` did. (4) The keyword parser and the model's anchor drop a leading language word ("Korean Parasite" → anchor Parasite, language ko; "French Kiss" kept whole). (5) An anchor that does not resolve is no longer a "Not used" word: the route asks "Which film did you mean?" with up to three typo-close titles (lib/search-typo.ts over lib/top-titles.ts) and ranks the rest of the ask.
